{% comment %}
Every step of the goal, with the actions already decided, each numbered and each property listed as
a blank to fill. One request per GOAL, not per step: the steps of a goal refer to one another
(`%!data%` is the action before it), and a model shown one step in isolation cannot see that.

The numbering is flat across the whole goal, so an answer keyed by number needs nothing
cross-referenced back.

Properties come from the action's own catalogue rows — name, type, required-or-not, default — so
nothing here restates what a class already declares about itself.
{% endcomment %}
{{ goal.Name }}
{% for s in goal.Step %}
step {{ s.Index }}: {{ s.Text }}
{%- for a in s.Decided %}
   {{ a.Number }}. {{ a.Module }}.{{ a.Name }}
   {%- for p in a.Property %}
      {{ p.Name }} ({{ p.Type.Name }}{% if p.Nullable %}, optional{% else %}, required{% endif %}{% if p.Default %}, default {{ p.Default }}{% endif %})
   {%- endfor %}
{%- endfor %}
{% endfor %}
